# This is a file of tests for the GMOS sequencer in a suitable format to be read
# by the tcsTests.tk procedure.
# 
# This particular test file is aimed at checking the input ranges to 
# the GMOS 'fltPos' CAD command.
#
#
# Comments are introduced by a # in the first column
# Blank lines can be left if required.
# The currently allowed keywords are (case is immaterial)
#
#  Test   <testId>
#  Command <commandName>
#  Field   <CAD field> <value>
#  Response Accept | Reject
#  Timeout <msecs>
#  OnError Continue | Abort
#  Log     <recordName>
#  Directive Start | Preset

# This first part before the first Test keyword can be used to setup 
# global values for Response, TimeOut and OnError. These global values
# can be over ridden within specific tests

Response Reject
TimeOut  30000
OnError  Continue

Help
Help These tests checks the trapping of invalid input to the
Help fltPos command.
Help
Help The first tests check for null input. If the commands in question have
Help been run at any time after booting and prior to running these tests then
Help there will already be input on the CAD fields and so these null tests
Help will fail. To validate the trapping of null input you will have to
Help reboot the GMOS sequencer and start these tests again.
Help
Help  The tests assume that a filter look-up table has been used
Help  that has a "blue" and a "red" filter on the same wheel
Help  but has a "blue" and a "purple" filter on different wheels.
Help
Help Press continue when ready
Help

# Tests start here. Each test must start with the Test keyword, end with
# a Directive keyword and have at least one Command keyword. Any Field
# keywords are assumed to apply to the last command

Test UT05010
Summary Check rejection of null input
Help Check rejection of null input

 Command fltPos 
 Field  DIR MARK   
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT05020
Summary Check rejection of unknown filter to first filter field
Help Check rejection of unknown filter to first filter field

 Command fltPos 
 Field  A  XXXXX
 Field  B  Hartmann_A
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT05030
Summary Check rejection of unknown filter to second filter field
Help Check rejection of unknown filter to second filter field

 Command fltPos 
 Field  A  red
 Field  B  XXXXX
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT05040
Summary Check rejection of unknown filter to both filter fields
Help Check rejection of unknown filter to both filter fields

 Command fltPos 
 Field  A  XXXXX
 Field  B  XXXXX
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT05050
Summary Check that the Sequencer reports CC rejection when both filters are on the same wheel
Help Check that the Sequencer reports CC rejection when both filters are on the same wheel
  Aftertest Pause

 Command fltPos 
 Field  A  Hartmann_A
 Field  B  Hartmann_B
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT05060
Summary Check acceptance of valid filter names
Help Check acceptance of valid filter names

Log c2:fltAssembly.A
Log c2:fltAssembly.B

 Command fltPos 
  Field  A  Hartmann_A
  Field  B  G2
  Response  Accept
  Directive Start

Test UT05070
Summary Check acceptance of further valid filter names
Help Check acceptance of further valid filter names

Log c2:fltAssembly.A
Log c2:fltAssembly.B

 Command fltPos 
  Field  A  Hartmann_B
  Field  B  I2
  Response  Accept
  Directive Start
